\pard\b\f0\fs24 The Icarus\b0\f1\fs18\par
\b\f0\par
Capacity:\b0\f1  Small corvette complement built around John's squad; exact numbers not stated.\par
\b\f0 Role in Story:\b0\f1  John's dependable drop ship and the team's main human vessel before the sentient transition.\par
\b\f0 Related Characters:\b0\f1  John Walker, Tao Vang, Shai Siante, Tex Kovachnikov.\par
\b\f0 Season:\b0\f1  Chapters 2-4.\par
\b\f0 Unique Features:\b0\f1  Old but battle-proven systems, extremely tight internal layout, and deep crew trust built on familiarity rather than novelty.\par
\b\f0 Description:\b0\f1  The Icarus is John's flag ship and the tightest corvette in the fleet. It lacks flashy specialist amenities, but John trusts it precisely because its older systems are dependable and familiar. It carries the squad through high-altitude insertions and remains the team's dependable human corvette during the lost-facility mission.\par
\b\f0 Sights:\b0\f1  Cold steel trusses, amber jump-light over the launch bay, cramped troop hold, and a hangar tight enough for Tex to complain about.\par
\b\f0 Sounds:\b0\f1  Engine hum, ramp mechanisms, launch-bay intercoms and gear clamps snapping into place.\par
\b\f0 Smell:\b0\f1  Cold metal, regulated air and machine oil.\par
\b\f0 Notes:\b0\f1  The manuscript's explicit self-healing hull sequence belongs to the Beverly, not the Icarus.\par
\b\f0 Built at:\b0\f1  Protectant fleet service.\par
